# mix_audit ignore list - deliberately visible and reasoned, not a silent
# suppression (requirements-rules.md §12.3: a confirmed finding SHOULD stay
# visible rather than be hidden, the same discipline as leaving a
# reviewed-clean static-analysis finding in place rather than deleting it).
#
# Both entries below are in cowlib (transitive, via plug_cowboy -> cowboy),
# currently pinned to 2.18.0 - the LATEST available version at the time
# this was reviewed (checked via `mix hex.info cowlib`; no newer, fixed
# release exists to bump to instead). Re-check this file whenever cowlib is
# upgraded - these entries should be removed once a real fix ships.

# EEF-CVE-2026-43969 / CVE-2026-43969 / GHSA-g2wm-735q-3f56 (LOW) - cookie
# request-header injection via cow_cookie:cookie/1's unvalidated encoder.
# The advisory's own affected range is 2.9.0-2.16.1 (last_affected:
# 2.16.1); our locked 2.18.0 is past that range and mix_audit's local
# database entry appears stale relative to the upstream OSV record
# (checked directly at https://api.osv.dev/v1/vulns/GHSA-g2wm-735q-3f56).
EEF-CVE-2026-43969

# EEF-CVE-2026-43966 / CVE-2026-43966 - HTTP response splitting via
# non-VCHAR bytes in cow_http_struct_hd:escape_string/2. This one has no
# upper bound in the advisory (still affects the latest release as of this
# review) - genuinely unpatched upstream, not a stale-database issue like
# the entry above. Accepted here because it's not exploitable through how
# this repo actually uses cowlib: the vulnerable path requires an
# application to pass attacker-controlled data into the low-level
# cow_http_struct_hd:item/1 structured-header builder directly, which
# neither Mix.Tasks.Server's StaticServerPlug nor Plug.Static do (they
# never construct custom structured HTTP headers from request input at
# all). The advisory itself also notes cowboy >= 2.16.0 already rejects
# CR/LF in outgoing header values by default via `invalid_response_headers`
# - we're on cowboy 2.17.0, so that default protection applies regardless.
EEF-CVE-2026-43966
